  "answer": "I don't have a shell tool available to execute tests, but I can verify the logic manually against each requirement and the public tests.\n\n**Verification against requirements:**\n\n1. **Type check**: `typeof input !== 'string'` throws `TypeError`. ✓\n2. **Split only on literal commas**: `input.split(',')`. ✓\n3. **Trim surrounding JS whitespace**: `.trim()` (uses JS whitespace definition). ✓\n4. **Collapse internal whitespace runs to one ASCII space**: `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')`. Note: `\\s` matches JS whitespace, and the replacement is a literal ASCII space. ✓\n5. **Lowercase with `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`**: `.toLowerCase()`. ✓\n6. **Discard empty normalized parts**: `if (normalized === '') continue;`. ✓\n7. **Unique in first-occurrence order, case-sensitive after normalization**: `Set` + push preserves order; since normalization lowercases, differently-cased spellings collapse to the same key and count as duplicates. ✓\n8. **Empty/delimiter-only returns `[]`**: all parts normalize to `''` and are skipped. ✓\n\n**Public tests trace:**\n- `'red,blue,green'` → `['red','blue','green']` ✓\n- `'  Red , , BLUE  ,'` → parts `'  Red '`→`'red'`, `' '`→`''`(skip), `' BLUE  '`→`'blue'`, `''`→`''`(skip) → `['red','blue']` ✓\n- `'Alpha,beta,alpha,BETA,gamma'` → `'alpha'`,`'beta'`,`'alpha'`(dup),`'beta'`(dup),`'gamma'` → `['alpha','beta','gamma']` ✓\n\n**Result:** Implemented `parseTags(input)` in `tags.mjs`, keeping the named export. The public tests in `public.test.mjs` were not modified. All three public tests pass by manual trace, and the implementation satisfies every stated requirement (TypeError on non-string, literal-comma split, trim, internal-whitespace collapse to a single ASCII space, `toLowerCase()`, empty-part discard, first-occurrence dedup, and `[]` for empty/delimiter-only input).",
